{
  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2023_W25_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-25",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2023_W25_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-25.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2023-06-23",
  "report_week": "25",
  "report_period": "Week 25 (16th Jun to 23rd Jun 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Ceres Shipping have committed their Capesize \"Aquaenna\" 176/2011 Jinhai, China (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) to Costamare for USD 22,4 mill. Remind you that back in April, the one-year-older \"Rosebank\" 177/2010 New Times, China (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 23,2 mill. Japanese owners have sold their Panamax \"Coral Opal\" 78/2012 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed buyers for low USD 19 mill. Note that the one-year-older \"Ultra Panache\" 78/2011 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 02/2026, DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 20,4 mill. The Ultramax \"Hanton Trader III\" 63/2014 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 11/2024, BWTS fitted) was committed at USD 23,6 mill. For comparison, the one-year- younger sister vessel \"Diomidis\" 63/2015 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in April at USD 25,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"Corinthian Emerald\" 57/2012 Stx, Korea (SS 03/2027, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) from Eurobulk was committed to Middle Eastern buyers for USD 17,25 mill. Moreover, the \"New Direction\" 56/2013 Mitsui, Japan (SS 06/2028, DD 04/2026, BWTS fitted) of Hsin Chien Marine was sold at USD 19,6 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"New Beginning\" 56/2013 Mitsui, Japan (SS 01/2028, DD 02/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold back in March at USD 20,5 mill. Newport have committed their Handysize \"Agia Irini\" 28/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 05/2024, BWTS fitted) to Florence Shipping for USD 13,8 mill. For reference, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Merchant Three\" 28/2012 Imabari, Japan (SS 10/2027, DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in March at low USD 13 mill.",
    "tankers": "The LR1 \"Faros\" 75/2005 Hyundai, Korea (SS 09/2025, DD 12/2023) of Benetech Shipping was committed to Turkish buyers Beks for region USD 18 mill. For comparison, the sisters \"Gulf Coast\", \"Gulf Horizon\" & \"Gulf Pearl\" 75/2005 (SS 11/2025, DD 12/2023 & SS 07/2025, DD 10/2023 & SS 04/2025, DD 07/2023, BWTS fitted) were sold a month ago at USD 20,4 mill each. The MR2 \"Anfa\" 48/2010 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed at low-mid USD 24 mill. Remind you that back in April, the one- year-older \"Dee4 Elm\" 47/2009 Onomichi, Japan (SS/DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 25 mill. In addition, the \"Gulf Jumeirah\" 46/2008 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 12/2023, DD 11/2023) of Gulf Energy Maritime was sold for mid USD 23 mill, while the \"Eagle Bay\" 47/2008 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 02/2028, DD 01/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold earlier this month at USD 24,2 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low/mid usd 8,00's fio range. Continental trips via East Coast Canada into Far East were fixed around usd 44,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 9,000/11,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 11,000/13,000 pd range. A number of Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/13,000 pd. Continental trips via North Coast South America into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 8,000/9,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via North Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 480K/675K. A Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 13,000 pd basis delivery China for 9/11 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 9,000/11,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 10,000/12,000 pd range. South East Asian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 9,000/12,000 pd. Trips from Philippines into China with nickel ore were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. West African trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 10,000/13,000 pd. US Gulf trips into India were reported at the level of usd 14,000 pd. South American Coastal trips were fixed around usd 12,000/13,000 pd. South American trips into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 12,000/15,000 pd. South American trips into India were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 450K/550K. South American trips into South East Asia were reported at the level of usd 12,000/13,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 280K/300K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A generally quiet week for this segment. A number of trips from Japan into Persian Gulf with steels were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. South East Asian trips into China were fixed around usd 7,000/8,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
